<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  EasyVox's third-party notices. Generated by scripts/notices.sh (cargo-about, with
  packaging/about.toml and this template) from Cargo.lock: edit those, not the HTML.
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>EasyVox: third-party notices</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; --muted: #666; --rule: #ddd; --code: #f5f5f5; }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --muted: #aaa; --rule: #444; --code: #222; } }
    body { font: 15px/1.5 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px; }
    h1 { font-size: 26px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    h2 { font-size: 19px; margin-top: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 4px; }
    h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 28px 0 4px; }
    p.lead, .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: 3px 8px 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
    pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: var(--code); padding: 12px; font-size: 12px; border-radius: 6px; max-height: 320px; overflow-y: auto; }
    ul.used-by { font-size: 13px; columns: 2; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Third-party notices</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    EasyVox is free software under the MIT License (LICENSE.txt, next to this file in
    EasyVox.app/Contents/Resources). It's built on the open-source software below, whose licenses
    ask that their notices travel with the app. The speech models aren't part of the app: EasyVox
    downloads them when you choose one, and its About page credits each of them.
  </p>

  <h2>Code inside the app that a crate's license doesn't name</h2>

  <h3>transcribe.cpp and ggml</h3>
  <p>
    The speech runtime, vendored in the <code>transcribe-cpp-sys</code> crate:
    transcribe.cpp (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 The transcribe.cpp authors) and
    ggml (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors).
    Their license texts are under MIT below. Two parts of ggml carry their own MIT notices in their
    file headers: <code>ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp</code>,
    Copyright 2024 Mozilla Foundation, and the YaRN rotary embedding in
    <code>ggml-cpu/ops.cpp</code> and <code>ggml-metal/kernels/rope.metal</code>,
    Copyright (c) 2023 Jeffrey Quesnelle and Bowen Peng. Both are under this license:
  </p>
  <pre>Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software
and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal in the Software without
restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the
Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or
substantial portions of the Software.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT
NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT
OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.</pre>

  <h3>miniz</h3>
  <p>
    Also vendored in <code>transcribe-cpp-sys</code>: miniz (MIT,
    Copyright 2013-2014 RAD Game Tools and Valve Software,
    Copyright 2010-2014 Rich Geldreich and Tenacious Software LLC). Its license text is under MIT below.
  </p>

  <h3>Lucide icons</h3>
  <p>
    The icons in the <code>gpui-kit-assets</code> crate are Lucide icons (ISC,
    Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors). Some of them come from Feather (MIT,
    Copyright (c) 2013-present Cole Bemis). Both texts are below, under ISC and MIT.
  </p>

  <h3>SQLite</h3>
  <p>
    History is kept in SQLite, built into the app through the <code>libsqlite3-sys</code> crate.
    SQLite is in the public domain (<a href="https://sqlite.org/copyright.html">sqlite.org/copyright.html</a>).
  </p>

  <h3>The Rust standard library</h3>
  <p>
    Built into the app, under MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option. Copyright the Rust Project
    Developers (<a href="https://github.com/rust-lang/rust">github.com/rust-lang/rust</a>).
  </p>

  <h3>Source code under the Mozilla Public License</h3>
  <p>These crates are used unchanged. Their source code is at the links given:</p>
  <ul>
    {{#each licenses}}{{#if (eq id "MPL-2.0")}}{{#each used_by}}
    <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}: <a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}{{/if}}">{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}{{/if}}</a>, and <a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}</a></li>
    {{/each}}{{/if}}{{/each}}
  </ul>

  <h2>Licenses in use</h2>
  <ul>
    {{#each overview}}
    <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a>: {{count}}</li>
    {{/each}}
  </ul>

  <h2>Crates</h2>
  <p class="muted">Every Rust crate compiled into the app, with its license and where its source is.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Crate</th><th>Version</th><th>License</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{#each crates}}
      <tr data-crate="{{package.name}}@{{package.version}}"><td>{{package.name}}</td><td>{{package.version}}</td><td>{{license}}</td><td><a href="{{#if package.repository}}{{package.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{package.name}}{{/if}}">{{#if package.repository}}{{package.repository}}{{else}}crates.io{{/if}}</a></td></tr>
      {{/each}}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>License texts</h2>
  {{#each licenses}}
  {{#if first_of_kind}}<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>{{/if}}
  <p class="muted">Used by:</p>
  <ul class="used-by">
    {{#each used_by}}
    <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
    {{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre>{{text}}</pre>
  {{/each}}
</body>
</html>
